        "en" to GemDetails(
            "Diamond is pure carbon crystallised in the Earth's mantle, 150 to 200 km deep, at 900 to 1,300 °C and a pressure of about 50,000 atmospheres. Most diamonds are between 1 and 3.5 billion years old. They were carried very quickly to the surface by deep volcanic eruptions that formed kimberlite or lamproite pipes. Erosion of these pipes later scattered some of the crystals into rivers and along coastlines, forming alluvial and marine deposits.",
